I implemented rotation for the tetromino pieces using the up arrow key. The rotation is performed around the first block of the current piece, applying a 90-degree clockwise transformation to each block's relative position. The new position is validated to ensure it stays within the game boundaries and does not collide with existing locked blocks.

Next recommended increment: Implement line clearing (detecting and removing completed rows, shifting rows above down) and add a game-over condition when a new piece cannot be placed at the spawn position.
